Subject: [PATCH 117/148] [ae-patch] List the admin's shared Claude accounts in
 every account picker and fetch a shared token at launch

So a second AE user's host can use company-paid Claude accounts that the
admin manages, without copying tokens between hosts (omnigent-ae, 2026-10-20).

A shared account is known to a host only by its id, shared:<name>; host
account names cannot hold a colon, so the two never collide. Selecting one
stores just the id as the host's active account. At launch account_env()
asks the server's GET /v1/ae/claude-accounts/shared/<name>/token with the
runner's own server credential and puts the token in the launch
environment only; OMNIGENT_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT carries the id for the status
line. Claude login detection counts a shared pick without fetching. A fork
may pick a shared account the source host does not list, checked against
the server's store through a resolver the omnigent-ae package registers.

Web: useDetectedCredentials adds the server's shared accounts after the
host's own logins; the account picker and the fork dialog mark them with a
Shared tag (Tabler users-group) and offer no rename.
